<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Cookie Policy for FC Mobile Tools by TanzimFC.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / COOKIES</p>
    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: September 19, 2026</p>

    <section><h2>1. What cookies are</h2><p>Cookies are small pieces of information stored in a browser by a website or third-party service. Similar technologies can include local storage and other browser-side mechanisms.</p></section>

    <section id="privacy-choices"><h2>2. Privacy choices and consent</h2><p>FCMOBILETOOLS uses one site-wide privacy choice experience so visitors see the same general controls across the website. Depending on the services active on the site, the consent experience can cover analytics, advertising, and similar non-essential technologies.</p><p>For Google advertising and related Google products, FCMOBILETOOLS may use Google's Privacy &amp; messaging consent solution and supported consent signaling. Where applicable, this can include the IAB Europe Transparency and Consent Framework for the regions and services covered by Google's policies.</p><p>Use the <strong>Privacy Choices</strong> link in the site footer to reopen the available consent controls.</p></section>

    <section><h2>3. Analytics cookies and similar technologies</h2><p>FCMOBILETOOLS uses Google Analytics on public pages. Google Analytics can use cookies and similar technologies to measure traffic, page usage, technical information, and aggregate site activity. The site is configured to provide a denied-by-default Google consent state for non-essential storage until an applicable consent signal is supplied by the configured consent solution.</p></section>

    <section><h2>4. Authentication cookies</h2><p>The private admin and creator workspaces use HTTP-only, secure session cookies to keep authorized users signed in. These cookies are operational/security cookies for restricted areas rather than public advertising cookies. They have limited lifetimes and are cleared when the relevant session is logged out or expires.</p></section>

    <section><h2>5. Local storage</h2><p>Some tools and legacy features store progress, predictions, settings, balances, quiz state, or similar information in your browser's local storage. This is designed to keep tool state on your device. Clearing site data can remove that progress.</p></section>

    <section><h2>6. Third-party resources</h2><p>Public pages may load resources from third parties such as Google services and Cloudinary. External websites you open from links, including YouTube, Discord, X, EA services, and others, may set their own cookies or use similar technologies under their own policies.</p></section>

    <section><h2>7. Managing cookies and storage</h2><p>You can block, delete, or manage cookies and local storage through your browser settings. Some private authentication and site functionality may stop working correctly if required cookies or browser storage are blocked or cleared.</p></section>

    <section><h2>8. Changes</h2><p>We may update this policy when our analytics, authentication, tools, hosting, or third-party integrations change. The date above identifies the current version.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
